Step-by-step to add Environment Variables
Step 1 — open Elastic Beanstalk

Go to:

AWS Console → Elastic Beanstalk

Click your application.

Example:

iris-beanstalk-env
Step 2 — open configuration

Click:

Configuration

You will see different sections.

Find:

Software

Click:

Edit
Step 3 — add environment variables

Scroll to:

Environment properties

Add variables one by one.

Click Add environment property

Add:

Name	Value
PORT	3000
AWS_REGION	ap-southeast-2
SAGEMAKER_ENDPOINT_NAME	iris-endpoint-103616
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID	your_new_access_key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY	your_new_secret_key
MODEL_PROVIDER	sagemaker
Example entry

Name:

AWS_REGION

Value:

ap-southeast-2

Click Add

Step 4 — save

Click:

Apply

Beanstalk will update environment (takes ~1 minute).

Step 5 — test

Open:

http://YOUR-BEANSTALK-URL/health
